# Trivy CVE exceptions for orkyo-community
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # Impact | Reason | Added: YYYY-MM-DD | Review: YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Policy: time-bound only. Review date must be within 14 days of added date.
# Remove entries once the upstream fix is available.

# ── nginx:1.31-alpine — libexpat 2.8.2-r0, fix 2.8.4-r0 not yet published ──────
# 2026-09-02: every published nginx-alpine line still ships libexpat 2.8.2-r0. Verified
# by scanning the live floating tags rather than the pinned digest: nginx:1.31-alpine,
# nginx:mainline-alpine and nginx:alpine all carry 2.8.2-r0, and the newest 1.31-alpine
# digest is package-identical to the one pinned here — a digest bump does not clear this.
# There is no 1.32-alpine line. Both are denial of service, and this nginx serves static
# assets only: it parses no attacker-supplied XML. `apk upgrade` is not an option — see
# CLAUDE.md. Clears itself when upstream rebuilds.
# The three 2026-07-09 entries that stood here (CVE-2026-56131/56407/56408) are gone: their
# fix was 2.8.2-r0, which the image now ships.
CVE-2026-66046  # HIGH | libexpat DoS through 2.8.3 (2.8.2-r0, fix 2.8.4-r0) | no published nginx-alpine rebuilt with 2.8.4-r0 yet | Added: 2026-09-02 | Review: 2026-09-16
CVE-2026-76641  # HIGH | libexpat <2.8.3-2 (2.8.2-r0, fix 2.8.4-r0) | no published nginx-alpine rebuilt with 2.8.4-r0 yet | Added: 2026-09-02 | Review: 2026-09-16

# ── Trivy false positive ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Trivy reports fix as 12.6.5 but KC ships mssql-jdbc 13.2.1.jre11 (newer); false positive.
CVE-2025-59250  # HIGH | mssql-jdbc: improper input validation — Trivy lists fix as 12.6.5 but KC ships 13.2.1.jre11 (newer); false positive | Added: 2026-05-21 | Review: 2026-08-08

# ── Alpine openssl 3.5.7-r0 — every base image, all container builds ───────────
# 2026-08-27: Alpine 3.23 and 3.24 both ship openssl 3.5.7-r0; the fix is 3.5.8-r0,
# which no published upstream image contains yet — verified 2026-08-27 by scanning
# the live floating tags, not just the pinned digests: mcr dotnet {aspnet,runtime}
# :10.0-alpine and nginx:1.31-alpine both still carry 3.5.7-r0, so a digest bump
# does not clear this. Reported against libcrypto3 and libssl3 under one CVE id.
# Impact here is a denial of service, not code execution, and every listener is
# behind Cloudflare and the nginx reverse proxy rather than exposed directly.
# `apk upgrade` is not an option — see CLAUDE.md. Clears itself when upstream
# rebuilds: nightly security-refresh.yml picks the new package up.
CVE-2026-14456  # HIGH | openssl DoS via unbounded memory (libcrypto3/libssl3 3.5.7-r0, fix 3.5.8-r0) | no upstream alpine image rebuilt with 3.5.8-r0 yet | Added: 2026-08-27 | Review: 2026-09-10

# ── Keycloak base OS layer ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2026-09-03: the KC-26.6.x-era entries that stood in this file (jackson-databind,
# micrometer, OpenJDK, libacl, pgjdbc, six netty, a jackson-core GHSA, and the two sqlite
# FTS5 ones) are gone from the image this repo actually ships — the nightly security refresh
# rebuilt the foundation KC base out from under them. Verified against the artifact CI scans,
# ghcr.io/kymr10n/orkyo-community-keycloak:sha-b1290a37, both with CI's flags and with
# --ignore-unfixed OFF: the only findings are the mssql-jdbc false positive above and the
# entry below.
CVE-2026-22020  # HIGH | java-21-openjdk-headless in the Keycloak 26.7.2 base image | no fixed package published upstream (Trivy reports no fix); arrived with the 26.7.2 bump that closes CVE-2026-18963 (CRITICAL account takeover) | Added: 2026-08-29 | Review: 2026-09-26
